{{!--
  One item tile, shared by all four panels of the shop — the character's pack, the Trader's
  stock, and the two staging columns. A single partial so an item cannot look like two different
  things depending on which column it is sitting in.

  **Icon only.** No name, no price under the box: at 72px a name is either clipped to
  uselessness or tall enough to halve how many items fit on screen, and the hover tooltip
  carries the full item card anyway. The name still lives on `data-name`, which is what the
  panel search filters against, and in the button's `aria-label`, which is what a screen reader
  announces.

  Rarity is a class rather than an inline colour (`rarity-veryrare`), keyed on the normalised
  rarity from `config.mjs#normalizeRarity` so it matches the shared palette. Colour is never the
  only cue: the tooltip names the rarity in words.

  Context (one entry from a panel's `tiles`):
    id, uuid, name, img
    rarity      normalised key, or "" for mundane gear
    qty         stock/held count; omitted when 1
    unlimited   true to show an infinity badge instead of a count
    price       pre-formatted price string, used in the label rather than on the face
    staged      how many of this line are currently in the stage
    blocked     true when the Trader will not trade this at all; the tile is disabled
    categories  space-separated category tokens ("equipment equipment:heavy") for the panel's
                type filter
    blockedWhy  localised reason, shown on hover — a greyed tile with no explanation is a bug
                report waiting to happen
    exhausted   true when every unit is already on the counter. Dimmed but **not** disabled:
                a disabled button receives no mouse events, and the right-click menu has to reach
                it to put the item back
    sourceUuid  the compendium entry "View item" opens — see `data/stock.mjs#sourceUuid`

  **No click action.** A single click does nothing; a double-click puts one on the counter, and
  the right-click menu and dragging are wired on the window — see `ShopApp#wireItemGestures`. The
  button is the draggable part rather than the list item, because it is the box the player sees
  and grabs; the icon inside is not draggable itself, or the browser would drag the picture.
    equipped    the character is wearing or wielding it (pack tiles only)
    attuned     the character is attuned to it (pack tiles only)
    statusNote  both of those in words, for the label — the icons are not the only cue
--}}
<li class="shop-tile{{#if rarity}} rarity-{{rarity}}{{/if}}{{#if staged}} is-staged{{/if}}{{#if blocked}} is-blocked{{/if}}{{#if exhausted}} is-exhausted{{/if}}"
    data-item-id="{{id}}" data-uuid="{{uuid}}" data-source-uuid="{{sourceUuid}}" data-name="{{name}}"
    data-categories="{{categories}}">

  <button type="button" class="shop-tile-button" data-item-id="{{id}}"
          {{#if blocked}}disabled{{else}}{{#unless exhausted}}draggable="true"{{/unless}}{{/if}}
          {{#if blocked}}data-tooltip="{{blockedWhy}}"{{else}}data-tooltip="{{shopItemTooltip uuid}}"{{/if}}
          aria-label="{{name}}{{#if price}} — {{price}}{{/if}}{{#if statusNote}} — {{statusNote}}{{/if}}{{#if exhaustedNote}} — {{exhaustedNote}}{{/if}}">
    <img class="shop-tile-img" src="{{img}}" alt="" draggable="false">

    {{#if unlimited}}
    <span class="shop-tile-badge" aria-label="{{localize 'sogrom-simple-dnd5e-magic-shop.stock.unlimited'}}">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i>
    </span>
    {{else if qty}}
    <span class="shop-tile-badge">{{qty}}</span>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if staged}}<span class="shop-tile-staged">{{staged}}</span>{{/if}}

    {{!-- Top right, clear of the staged badge (top left) and the count (bottom right). The same
          icons dnd5e's own inventory uses, so they need no learning. --}}
    {{#if (or equipped attuned)}}
    <span class="shop-tile-status" aria-hidden="true">
      {{#if equipped}}<i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i>{{/if}}
      {{#if attuned}}<i class="fa-solid fa-sun"></i>{{/if}}
    </span>
    {{/if}}
  </button>
</li>
